 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse of the veterinarian directory: a specialty view that answers "which veterinarians hold this specialty". It lists every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, and under each specialty the veterinarians who hold it, each shown by full name (first name first). Veterinarians who hold no specialty are gathered together under a "no specialty" grouping rather than omitted. The page is organized by specialty, not as a roster of veterinarians. Every specialty renders on a single page, without pagination `[REQ-VET-003]`. The page is reachable by its own address alone. No navigation entry and no link from another page belongs to this requirement — a visible entry point is deferred to a possible follow-up.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name, and under each the veterinarians who hold it are shown by full name with the first name before the last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears under a "no specialty" grouping.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties and veterinarians, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty and the "no specialty" grouping render on one page, with no pagination.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed by its stored name, with no veterinarians shown beneath it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each specialty, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and the "no specialty" grouping holds a stable position among them.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
